1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,140
Listen to a talk in a music class.

2
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:07,100
You are probably all familiar with jazz music.

3
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:10,140
Its history begins in the southern United States.

4
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:15,082
It originated in the early 20th century in the city of New Orleans, blending

5
00:00:15,082 --> 00:00:19,220
elements of different kinds of music like African rhythms, blues, and ragtime.

6
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:24,150
One of the key characteristics of jazz is its emphasis on improvisation.

7
00:00:24,150 --> 00:00:30,140
Musicians often create spontaneous melodies and harmonies, making each performance unique.

8
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:35,240
This contrasts with classical music, where compositions are typically played as written.

9
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:38,414
Jazz musicians also use syncopation,

10
00:00:38,414 --> 00:00:44,040
which involves shifting the normal accents in the rhythm to create an unexpected and exciting sound.

11
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:49,455
In the 1920s, jazz became widely popular and moved north to cities like Chicago

12
00:00:49,455 --> 00:00:50,180
and New York City.

13
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:55,857
During the Jazz Age, as this period became known, famous jazz musicians like Louis

14
00:00:55,857 --> 00:00:58,144
Armstrong became household names,

15
00:00:58,144 --> 00:01:00,190
and jazz clubs flourished as social hubs.

16
00:01:00,190 --> 00:01:07,120
Over time, jazz continued to evolve, in part by incorporating elements from other musical traditions and cultures.

17
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:13,090
Today, it remains a vibrant and influential genre, celebrated for its creativity and expressive power.

18
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:13,140
Next, we will look at the impact of jazz on other musical genres

19
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:13,190
and how it has shaped contemporary music.
